{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he arose.</b> Rabbi Yeshua said: the men of the ship went to Nineveh and told Jonah's matter; therefore they believed, and the word לאלהים I have explained [accordingly]." "<b>A journey of three days.</b> Around the city is a journey of one day, from end to end; or he did not go to call throughout, but only a journey of one day, therefore."], :book :jonah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The referent of 'the word לאלהים' is uncertain; likely the phrase 'believed in Elohim' (Jonah 3:5), which Ibn Ezra says he explained in light of Rabbi Yeshua's account.", 1 "The word 'therefore' (על כן) at the end is textually abrupt; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Jonah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=19&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:07.167631562Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}